{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731057Z","id":"487dd91624f77a276deb8f3ecfe7963392c43620da67d0e2082724611e817b40","body":{"detail":"The gallery topic is shared by every viewer, so it cannot carry this viewer's attention (addressed threads, new replies, open threads): a version, thread or thread_deleted event there still fetches the viewer's attention on that one artifact, and a card's roster (participants) is only as fresh as the last full fetch (going live, resync, and every SAFETY_MS).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"7bdd3932434a71d1ad19e2be45e3bcc78fc1aeb1b9b1eb6f901e3465908a0ac1"},"suggested_fix":"A per-viewer topic, or attention computed from the thread summary, would remove the fetch.","summary":"The gallery fetches this viewer's attention per event","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381871Z","id":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"5db66b848687622e5d49e34f29d62226d5e43b73a103486a2ad57576b2d27af4"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378103Z","id":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","body":{"detail":"The box re-implements the stage composer's target line, status line, focus on render, Escape to close, Cmd/Ctrl+Enter to post and the busy state (Composer.svelte). Rendering Composer.svelte from this lazy chunk makes the artifact entry export it, which adds 5 gzip bytes to an entry that sits exactly at its budget (63988 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json, measured by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs). A behaviour change to the stage composer (a post queued while a screenshot is taken, the keyboard-trail guard, the live status region) must be mirrored here by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"072d1faa169ad8499be271406d7ad89a490cbb4a88f0a1450fc3c964f840da26"},"suggested_fix":"Render Composer.svelte here once the artifact entry has a few bytes of slack, or move Composer.svelte's form into a component both import.","summary":"The New comment box repeats Composer.svelte's form instead of rendering it","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry has slack under its bundle budget","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378379Z","id":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","body":{"detail":"The panel's first child stays the questions slot (shell/src/sidebar.test.ts 'puts the questions about the page at the top' asserts it), so an agent's question to the viewer still leads; the box comes next, above the working strips, the batch-send button and every thread. Putting the box first means changing that rule and its test.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"fef8ce9785f9ab52019fb078c2e7a3d70f61d7555644dc6354c03c421220d211"},"summary":"The New comment box sits below the questions for the viewer, not first in the panel","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562354Z","id":"a1183f70422a18f50596fd21afab39b387b08d9efb06a2812ce2fcf243100d3f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffd6520","summary":"NewComment.svelte now renders Composer.svelte with wholeDraft(); the artifact entry's budget rose by the 18 gzip bytes this costs (63988 to 64006). Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/new-comment.test.ts` passes (6 tests, the composer opened in place), `node scripts/bundle-size.mjs` passes at artifact 64006, and e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts passes.","supersedes":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562538Z","id":"34e47162a05b76ffccf89f11259da17f6f73e72bedf6bea858a49095e6fad068","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the coordinator of this work: the box stays below the questions slot, since questions to the viewer are time-sensitive and lead the panel. No change.","supersedes":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:46:08.079116Z","id":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent calls ask; the question reaches Sam's inbox (GET /api/inbox as Sam's cookie lists it) but Sam's shell shows 'The inbox is its owner's' at /inbox and loads no question card, so the agent waits until its timeout. Sam's shell never subscribes to the questions or inbox topic, so Hub::holds_surface for Sam is never true and every hook question of Sam's agents goes to the terminal. The server side (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs, routes/questions.rs) already serves a connected person; no plan task wires the shell for one. Plan Task 21 now carries this: gate the inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics on 'owner or connected person' (a 200 from /api/inbox), verified in a real browser as a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"4fa564c24b6a3357c8558f6fe29f63e75f25d8a83c205bb99a84e03fb763bc20"},"suggested_fix":"Gate the inbox page and the q module on 'owner or connected person' (GET /api/inbox answering 200 rather than ownerBrowser()), and verify /inbox and a question card in a real browser as a connected person.","summary":"A connected person's browser has no inbox or question surface: /inbox tells them the inbox is the owner's, and the q module loads only for the owner","tags":["review","task:21","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.856081Z","id":"31b2b5407e05366873abebfca2258736dba7844357defeaba91b5e1a253ee62e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","summary":"/people now loads its page the same way (web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts peoplePage, its own chunk, measured as `people` by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs); no perf gate times /people either.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878654Z","id":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","body":{"detail":"The banner is a floating pill at the foot of the stage (16px from the bottom), the .banner pattern of theme.css. At the top (where .banner sits by default) it covered the page's heading and, at 390px, the first changed element; the hosted prototype (hosted/ui/src/components/DraftBanner.svelte) is a full-width strip above the frame that takes height from it. The foot can cover a page's last lines and sits where the gesture hint shows.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"644f2b09adf7dcedf95daab24d7542db8db7e82c9a37a148efbeab6614c89fcf"},"summary":"Draft banner at the foot of the stage rather than the top or a strip that pushes the frame down","tags":["drafts","ui","revisit:a page's footer controls are hidden by the banner","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.647490Z","id":"4030afed5afdf271dc22537c9e49bc1157f338b3ec018a7461711e6fc05d8cfa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","summary":"Kept at the foot of the stage, the place branch rust-live-seats gives its spectator banner for the same reason (a top banner hid the page heading); the foot is now one stacking container, .stage-foot (StageIsland.svelte, theme.css), holding the gesture hint and the draft banner so neither covers the other","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.647553Z","id":"7526ffb5df8d2df3fc177d8b654590a3d2cf6562c6dd25a686832b6b951b4bd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a88e5379","summary":"Decided by a88e5379: the banner stays at the stage's foot inside .stage-foot. Browser-checked at 1280 and 390, light and dark (a hint added to .stage-foot sits above the banner, its bottom at or above the banner's top; no horizontal scroll); `npx playwright test e2e/drafts.spec.ts` passes","supersedes":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/StageIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.648984Z","id":"21794a99a26fde0b2a4231041bbdf1cfa7ef184eb9db24533ba8504a9e0dddc1","body":{"detail":"rust-live-seats renders <div class=\"banner spectate\"> in StageIsland.svelte as a sibling of the notice banner, placed by theme.css `.banner.spectate { top: auto; bottom: 16px; z-index: 5 }` (and a 480px rule with left/right 16px). This branch's draft banner sits in .stage-foot, also 16px from the stage's bottom. Move the spectate div inside <div class=\"stage-foot\"> (after the draft banner, or before it to sit above); `.stage-foot > .banner` makes it static, so its bottom/left/right/transform rules go inert and can be dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"48185f62b30f9dab3fe46869f78c48bb69e87ddbdab4c8e996d4b91fcb18865b"},"summary":"Merging rust-live-seats: its spectator banner must move into .stage-foot or it overlaps the draft banner","tags":["drafts","ui","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/StageIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:08.575739Z","id":"08a2346e4e63c593dd20b5ebcbb4e15b6594a324fbba3ef3788f042144006bfa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:83ad7424","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"055d37c636889e67b2609d0bc9ccd1c9b6c9d925268b06dd453ad7efe3c69026"},"summary":"The spectate banner renders inside .stage-foot after the draft banner; theme.css drops its own bottom/left/right/transform placement and stretches it at 480px. Measured with both shown: at 1280x800 the draft banner ends at y=738 and the spectator banner starts at y=746; at 390x844, 711 and 719. e2e/seats.spec.ts and e2e/drafts.spec.ts pass","supersedes":"21794a99a26fde0b2a4231041bbdf1cfa7ef184eb9db24533ba8504a9e0dddc1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.671412Z","id":"a4d376824b3e5f61e21fa3da60b170d381d4a4ca12672ba5a4913c3736c5920d","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:49:03.386685Z","id":"844c615e910a083e7ad3006cae8c9b68740d6e50dc5129453a04ca3c03fc7699","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.167408Z","id":"bb5952b279110eb432399d1781ba20bd9405c9fd6dcb56bdb085522d1da5dcce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9cfb85d5","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"39ac376e501ae839340948c725b0c74fbe8a809c02556d58def8f9d2444bcf45"},"summary":"The inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics load in any browser GET /api/inbox answers (inboxBrowser in web/shell/src/owner.ts), in the gallery and the artifact view. Evidence: gallery.test.ts 'gives a connected person's browser its inbox at /inbox, Inbox in the header, and the inbox and questions topics' passes, and e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts passes: Sam's browser at the LAN address shows his inbox, and his answer to his agent's ask reaches the agent's clax mcp.","supersedes":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.168179Z","id":"b9b2cafad146ac28ee85b03a8e99ec0a102fbfe21d4bee58c39c7ec839ab8be0","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"8562287422b69247ef5172e2996d8000dd4a834547e2eec0f95c600f71de4284"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815322Z","id":"a41a081a026386a88b9b7c4791858f7a18e9136c79a6a73c6f7927b13532f26d","body":{"detail":"The card is shown while the thread's delivery state is withheld; deciding releases the thread, so the card (and the outcome it shows, \"Allowed in this thread\") disappears with the next thread event, and the label changes to the delivery state. The inbox keeps decided cards in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a card decided here until the thread is collapsed or the view reloads.","summary":"The approval card above a thread leaves as soon as the decision lands","tags":["task:22","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.162875Z","id":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","body":{"detail":"Failure: a LAN viewer comments on a thread, the owner replies '+1', and the owner sends the thread to Sam's agent (Sam lets the owner's content reach his agents). Sam gets an open routing request for the LAN viewer's comment (GET /api/approvals/requests) and his inbox strip says '2 approvals' for two such threads, but the thread's feedback_state is 'sent': the owner's card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent' and Sam's artifact view shows no approval card above the thread, because the card is gated on feedback_state.state === 'withheld' (here) and the daemon derives that state from the thread's latest forwarded comment only (FEEDBACK_STATES, crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1800-1822). Reproduced in Chromium on a scratch daemon at commit f7a89d53.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Show the card for every open thread with an open approval item for this viewer (thread-approvals.ts already fetches them per artifact), not only withheld ones; and have the thread's delivery state read withheld (with its approver) while any undelivered row of the thread is held under an open request, so the sender sees it too. Add a test with a two-comment thread whose first comment is held.","summary":"A thread whose newest comment reaches the agent hides its open approval request: no approval card above it, and its card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent'","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163617Z","id":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","body":{"detail":"The chip is capped at 45% of the card head with an ellipsis; a 32-character agent name ('clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab') is clipped at 1280 px, and for another person's agent the person after ' · ' is not visible at all at 390 px, where there is no hover. The title is only '<person>'s agent', so the clipped agent name cannot be read anywhere on the card.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"c4e0c89012c6eee44bb22a89549c9a94d4af865540ab76a4a3f1e6175bbff523"},"suggested_fix":"Make the title '<agent name>, <person>'s agent' (or 'your agent'), so hover and assistive tech get the whole name.","summary":"The owner chip's hover text never names the agent, and the chip clips both name and person","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.255042Z","id":"1bd4ebd4d659cd4ddb42d8f9957736b3bf60aa09f9814cc57131b7b9cdf29ad3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The thread's state reads withheld while any of its rows is held (state_of in crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs looks at every row, not only the newest comment's), and the sidebar puts the approval card above any sent thread with an open request of this viewer's, whatever its state. Evidence: api_approvals::a_thread_waits_for_approval_while_an_earlier_comment_is_held passes (LAN viewer comments, the owner replies '+1', the owner sends to Sam's agent: one request, state withheld, approver Sam), and fails with the old newest-comment-only check; thread-owner.test.ts 'puts the card above a thread whose newest comment went through while an earlier one waits' passes.","supersedes":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.257609Z","id":"cbe7729e9446a4831c5098169e7d9b1bb1ce82b0a84fd3a26218b148c6e02a5a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The chip's title names the agent whole: 'sam-web, Sam's agent' or 'clax-claude, your agent'. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts chip tests and web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts (title 'sam-notes, Sam's agent') pass.","supersedes":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/thread-approvals.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.261111Z","id":"ebcdef66dfc53597bba1d8df20f8ca720898ee76046645e10c2fb56511ab2687","body":{"detail":"approvalsFor asks /api/inbox?kind=approval&artifact=<aid>&limit=200 and keeps the open ones; on an artifact with more than 200 approval items for this viewer, an older open request gets no card above its thread (the inbox still lists it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"13ada5962992c59740f6e11d0f02bb133386432bd8365ed150f0f9331aed060c"},"suggested_fix":"Page through next_cursor, or have the inbox list filter approval items by request status.","summary":"The approval card above a thread reads the newest 200 approval items of the artifact, decided ones included","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317399Z","id":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","body":{"detail":"Failure: in Chromium at 390 px, Sam's view of a thread owned by the owner's agent named clax-multi-person shows the chip as 'clax-multi-person · …' (scrollWidth > clientWidth, also at 1280 px); the title 'clax-multi-person, Alex's agent' fixes the hover case (record da6f1bf9, closed by cbe7729e), but phones have no hover, so whose agent owns the thread cannot be read there. The chip is capped at max-width 45% (line 194).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"27e61d3c10a083f476b2a112151790172f0799095acedb50608d859b2ab40a12"},"suggested_fix":"Let the chip wrap below the anchor at narrow widths, or clip the agent name and keep ' · <person>' whole.","summary":"At phone width another person's name on the owner chip is still cut off; only the hover title names it","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317441Z","id":"a710d7eecc9218b901a639296bbb61efbf8a94b3e52b6336f5b5a5f4d7372f36","body":{"detail":"Failure: a LAN viewer (not connected) opens the Send menu at /a/<aid> and the browser logs 'Failed to load resource: the server responded with a status of 403 (Forbidden)' for GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/approves-first each time. The shell already knows the viewer is neither the owner nor a person (ShellSidebar.svelte tests s.me?.owner || s.me?.person for the approval card).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"33cdbc519d7c246d7aa0d91cd784c4d1093cac91f79b0385e460b50630690b35"},"suggested_fix":"Pass aid/threads to SendButton only when the viewer is the owner or a connected person.","summary":"Every Send menu a LAN viewer opens asks approves-first and logs a 403 to the console","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317485Z","id":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner on an artifact where only Sam's agent is live, with two unsent threads, sees no send-unsent button (Chromium 1280 and 390 px); each card's Send and the selection bar's 'Send 2 to …' open the menu, but sending all unsent needs ticking every card. The `!pick` guard hides the button instead of letting it open the same menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"5afef93bda6e86ed7909748b307da430ec354804c2a44df3cb682934a86b0fc8"},"summary":"With only other people's agents live, the 'Send N unsent' button is gone rather than opening the menu","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"e176c69ecad624feebfeeb2f5d53fc02bc872b7ed695f77504ff7f0d3f4f597b","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":226},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","supersedes":"a4d376824b3e5f61e21fa3da60b170d381d4a4ca12672ba5a4913c3736c5920d","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ed95ead8f0d830facc04622854415fa962f9cec9c747915ce56c1d6df667fc77","body":{"detail":"Failure: in Chromium at 390 px, Sam's view of a thread owned by the owner's agent named clax-multi-person shows the chip as 'clax-multi-person · …' (scrollWidth > clientWidth, also at 1280 px); the title 'clax-multi-person, Alex's agent' fixes the hover case (record da6f1bf9, closed by cbe7729e), but phones have no hover, so whose agent owns the thread cannot be read there. The chip is capped at max-width 45% (line 194).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"27e61d3c10a083f476b2a112151790172f0799095acedb50608d859b2ab40a12"},"suggested_fix":"Let the chip wrap below the anchor at narrow widths, or clip the agent name and keep ' · <person>' whole.","summary":"At phone width another person's name on the owner chip is still cut off; only the hover title names it","supersedes":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ce0922d0c368a754793f82175342c92ecf9377e42204310df000e1e00ae1eaef","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","supersedes":"844c615e910a083e7ad3006cae8c9b68740d6e50dc5129453a04ca3c03fc7699","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"9707ea366fbf1f769915443fcab1a9779d8d3467e65af416f7c3472f23daec18","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"949ee66fbd902fe13b7116a027c0786aa4b813eb96be329d49c4922c2eac27cc"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"b9b2cafad146ac28ee85b03a8e99ec0a102fbfe21d4bee58c39c7ec839ab8be0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:41.935654Z","id":"fefd8d61ea66b578f29354e0cf77096dc743374838aba428d18dece9e2b378fd","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner on an artifact where only Sam's agent is live, with two unsent threads, sees no send-unsent button (Chromium 1280 and 390 px); each card's Send and the selection bar's 'Send 2 to …' open the menu, but sending all unsent needs ticking every card. The `!pick` guard hides the button instead of letting it open the same menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"cd09e7a9f4b87dd272c347479f75eec6ab3a4bee1f0e48a3feaf8696f6941321"},"summary":"With only other people's agents live, the 'Send N unsent' button is gone rather than opening the menu","supersedes":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:41.935654Z","id":"cb998259585aedc7e406cc2a6c766dbacdf1754811aea4dd027a8c901e13ff45","body":{"detail":"The card is shown while the thread's delivery state is withheld; deciding releases the thread, so the card (and the outcome it shows, \"Allowed in this thread\") disappears with the next thread event, and the label changes to the delivery state. The inbox keeps decided cards in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"6dff1646984c1a4b12213e009b773e3db44fdd942f8489665c6e24c3d58ce30a"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a card decided here until the thread is collapsed or the view reloads.","summary":"The approval card above a thread leaves as soon as the decision lands","supersedes":"a41a081a026386a88b9b7c4791858f7a18e9136c79a6a73c6f7927b13532f26d","tags":["task:22","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268853Z","id":"1472fc0cad9c4d1e801867fa41d307b3d59772bb3dc06f0ce8f200a0c8647eec","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cb998259585aedc7e406cc2a6c766dbacdf1754811aea4dd027a8c901e13ff45","summary":"Changed since recorded: the card above a thread is now shown while the thread is open and sent to an agent, to the owner or a connected person (web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte:33), not only while its delivery state is withheld, so a decision no longer removes it at the next thread event. Proposed close: reason:fixed, once someone confirms the decided card stays in a browser.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.660616Z","id":"98acc0e2e23308fe05f933939943e555c934e59c02bec4b8950b236db8b2041c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"The chip's agent name gives way (ellipsis) and ' · <person>' stays whole. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'lets the person on another person's agent's chip stay whole' passes; Chromium at 390 px shows 'clax-multi-person-… · Sam' (target/t22/shots-r2/owner-after-decline-long-chip-390-*).","supersedes":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.663322Z","id":"cdb9c60248fd8bdd74e300c0bfecf57b174db48e9fafd473ce7ba8a47b0b634f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"The sidebar hands SendButton the artifact to ask about only in the owner's or a connected person's browser. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'never asks who approves first in a browser that may not learn it' passes; web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts sees no approves-first request from the LAN viewer's menu.","supersedes":"a710d7eecc9218b901a639296bbb61efbf8a94b3e52b6336f5b5a5f4d7372f36","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.664240Z","id":"f036f9e5bdec61556b7b53479d475ae96e212e70e9991d881c4b74982c49dbfd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"With no target chosen, the unsent bar is a Send button that opens the menu ('Send 2 unsent to …'). Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'with only other people's agents live and no target' passes (the bar opens the menu); Chromium: target/t22/shots-r2/owner-unsent-bar-opens-menu-*.","supersedes":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657901Z","id":"cea8f8405733d61b549c25a3dddbb722ddee67727b7691afee0f9c8bd6a1e837","body":{"detail":"The label takes 'yours' (an open request of this viewer's on the thread) over the thread's feedback_state. Routing requests outlive their target (spec section 9.2 withdraws them only on resolve, delete, revocation, or the end of an asking session). Seen as the owner: (1) after the owner's codex session that Mia's thread waited for ended, the owner read 'waiting for your approval', and every other viewer read 'agent session ended; waiting for a new one'; (2) after the owner's claude agent handed Mia's thread to Sam's agent, the owner read 'waiting for your approval', while the server state was 'waiting for Sam's approval'. The server state follows StateRow::waits_for_approval (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1855-1867), which needs a live session. The approver's label does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"cc55684f277b54f807d8f3b1642d19c5389486e04176b23d17e46f36ada43d4f"},"summary":"The approver's card reads 'waiting for your approval' after the target session ended or the thread was handed off","tags":["review","people","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657949Z","id":"466b955af142f500e9759bebec441475f8de029fd47f0414f41222ebe3c2beac","body":{"detail":"Chromium at 1280 px, as the owner, once the Inbox button loads. The summary line '8 open threads · clax-multi-person-claude (Mia's), clax-multi-person (Sam's) idle' takes 444 px. It is white-space: nowrap, with no min-width: 0 or ellipsis. The page is 1298 px wide, and the theme switch is pushed 18 px past the viewport. At 1440 px it fits. Default agent names come from the repository and branch, so names this long are usual.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"fe41b1e8a8b817ef590fc159804a36aae40c8d69b9a5a193a2f281f911c3ae0d"},"summary":"The top bar overflows at 1280 px when the agent summary names two other people's agents","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Share.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.396129Z","id":"80f9b7c21dedfd94fab5ffe067c29c7d32bc92184de7d0743b990e886811c241","body":{"detail":"Share.svelte loads with the more menu after the first paint and asks sharing to decide whether to show Share. On a local daemon, which serves no /api/hosted route, that is one 404 per artifact view; on a hosted daemon one store read. It does not delay the first paint or comment mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"dbb107e1fe91721b632d7ece169ed3e065c0c10f9e6a63da75c13119b7805725"},"suggested_fix":"Carry can_share on GET /api/artifacts/<id> (the view already loads it) and drop the separate request.","summary":"Every artifact view asks GET /api/hosted/artifacts/<id>/sharing once after the first paint, and a local daemon answers it 404","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
